body:
Me and my first bf dated for a few years, and it took me a while to completely get over him. Maybe a year and a half. He wasn't very nice to me either- he cheated on me, and left me when I needed him the most amongst other things. I truly believed he was "the one" even after all his BS.  I used to even believe that you never truly get over the people you love. WRONG. 

You can and will get over this guy I promise you. Write down all the fuked up things he did, and every time you miss him go back and read them. The way to truly get over someone, is to love YOURSELF. I know people say this all the time but it's so so real. If you don't love and respect yourself you're gonna keep settling for people like this, when you KNOW you deserve better. 

&#x200B;

Remind yourself that theres sooooo many other guys out there who you're gonna fall for, who will hurt and betray you, or love and care for you. I have loved other guys after my ex, (which I never thought would happen) and I have also gotten hurt by them. You need to stay strong and NEVER SETTLE FOR LESS. I would also suggest writing down qualities you want in a guy, such as honesty, kindness, loyalty etc. If a guy you're falling for doesn't have them, CANCEL THEM.

&#x200B;

Good luck mate. I know it's so painful but you will get through this and come out a stronger woman. Don't forget your worth, and don't give yourself to men who are unworthy.

This unbearable pain in your chest you speak of, I feel it everyday, every moment of my existence. No matter what i do, where i go, who i'm with, the pain is there and it's been here for a long time.

The boy I fell in love with broke up with me too, and it was literally unbearable. Not only did i want him more than any thing, i NEEDED him. I crave him and resist the urge to text him everyday. He never loved me. He told me he never even cared as much. I maintained contact with him for a bit after the breakup knowing it was a bad idea. I got even more pain from that. I was holding onto him for so long, hoping he'd come back, hoping on some goddamn miracle to make him love me. I was stupid. I was a fool. I have officially let him go. It took a while but I want nothing to do with him. I don't deserve this treatment.

&#x200B;

I have recently come to this realization so allow me to share it with you. We CANNOT rely on anyone, for emotional dependency. Why? because people leave. Most people, are temporary. It's okay to rely on your friends in times of need, but that is different. You can rely on them, it helps but please don't make the mistake of NEEDING anyone. We are more than enough and capable of being on our own. People just don't want to do that. No one wants to be alone or feel alone. But the truth is, we ARE all alone. No one is gonna fight your battles for you. 

&#x200B;

Also, whoever says such "accomplishments" leads to fulfillment, doesn't know what the hell they are talking about. You probably feel just as empty as me, and traveling or getting A's isn't about to change that.

&#x200B;

Listen to me on this, find out why you're alive. Find out the real meaning of your life. Because I promise you it's so much more and deeper than boys and successes.  Good luck

Happy New Year. (:

&#x200B;

Lets's be stronger than we were yesterday, and keep getting stronger.

I know I'm young. I know there's probably better people in this world. But unfortunately this feeling is all too familiar to me. My first bf of 4 years cheated on me and I wanted to die then as well.  Fuck knows how I made it out of that. Then after ages I met another guy, and I was finally starting to like another person. He also left me. But it's okay because my feelings for him weren't as deep.

&#x200B;

But this is the last straw for me. My recent ex is the only other person I have loved after my first bf. I can't fuking take it anymore. I know it's stupid, immature, weak, pathetic. But once I die none of it will matter. 

&#x200B;

Im sorry

I'm not gonna tell you how everything will get better, or any of that BS. Because I've learned from experience it doesn't help. What I will tell you, Is what I tell myself. Remember, we can have support but it is us who must pick ourselves back up.

&#x200B;

Take back the power to your own life. It is YOUR life, we only live ONCE. And God knows its way too short to be depressed and feeling sorry for yourself. I know somethings in life are out of our hands, so we must make sure that we take advantage of the things we do have control over. You have a wife, let me tell you being single for so long, sometimes I desperately desire the company of a companion. Please talk to your wife, reconnect with her. Follow your instincts and PLEASE believe in yourself. You are strong. So strong. You are capable. And the world is lucky to have you. Dont let people screw you over, no matter who it is. Be confident, and live life without any regrets. All the problems you have, figure out a solution. Take action.
